# Eurovision LOOY experiment results (held-out, XGBoost, seed-averaged, leak-proof)

Protocol: hold-one-year-out over grand-final contests. Per fold: imputation,
label encoding, PCA, scaling all fit on train only; metrics on held-out years
only. Regularized xgboost (depth 3, lr 0.05, 200 rounds, reg_lambda 10,
subsample 0.8), predictions averaged over 5 seeds. Model trains on ALL train
rows per fold (no validation split). Cantobel-as-feature runs are excluded
(leaky: -0.89 corr with target).

Final numbers (5 seeds, rerun 2026-09-18):

## exp1: predict Rasch competitiveness (cantobel_median), 386 songs, 15 years
- full features (audio+lyrics+youtube+voting+running+country):
  median R2 0.241, pooled R2 0.245, mean MAE 0.557, mean Spearman 0.472
  - 2023 is a catastrophic distribution-shift fold (R2 -4.57); median or pooled
    is the defended aggregate.
  - baseline: Burgoyne audio embeddings explain 7.2% of competitiveness
    => pooled 0.245 = 3.4x the 7.2% benchmark
- no-youtube variant: median R2 0.085, pooled R2 0.111 (removes post-contest
  exposure signal; near baseline, as expected)

## exp2: predict grand-final ranking (place_contest_scaled), 411 songs, 16 years
- full features: median R2 0.174, pooled R2 0.186, mean avg_rank_error 6.10
  (paper approach 3: R2 0.09, ARE 6.80) => doubled R2, ARE 6.10 vs 6.80
- intrinsic+youtube (approach 2 equiv): median R2 0.163, pooled 0.137, ARE 6.35
  (paper approach 2: R2 0.30, ARE 4.96) => below paper's headline number
- no-youtube: median R2 0.043, pooled 0.031
- intrinsic only: R2 ~0 (music/lyrics alone carry no contest signal)

## takeaways for resume
- approach-3-equivalent contest-rank model beats paper: R2 0.09 -> ~0.19, ARE 6.8 -> ~6.1
- competitiveness model explains ~25% held-out variance, ~3.4x the 7.2% audio-only benchmark
